points.explanation:
The volitional form is the plain, casual version of {〜ましょう}. Use it with friends and family to suggest doing something together: {一緒[いっしょ]に帰[かえ]ろう} 'Let's go home together'. Said to yourself, it shows a decision made on the spot: {よし、がんばろう} 'Right, I'll give it my best'.

How to make it:

- {る}-verbs: drop {る}, add {よう}: {食[た]べる} → {食[た]べよう}, {寝[ね]る} → {寝[ね]よう}
- {う}-verbs: move the last sound to the o-row and add {う}: {書[か]く} → {書[か]こう}, {話[はな]す} → {話[はな]そう}, {待[ま]つ} → {待[ま]とう}, {飲[の]む} → {飲[の]もう}, {帰[かえ]る} → {帰[かえ]ろう}, {買[か]う} → {買[か]おう}
- Irregular: {する} → {しよう}, {来[く]る} → {来[こ]よう}

Add {か} to make a casual offer or suggestion, like {〜ましょうか}: {手伝[てつだ]おうか} 'Shall I help?'
